{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{5-3x}{x^2+3x}$ is a rational expression.\n\nTo find the derivative of rational expressions, we use **the quotient rule**:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}\\right]\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dx}[u(x)]v(x)-u(x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}[v(x)]}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{u'(x)v(x)-u(x)v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's differentiate!\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left(\\dfrac{5-3x}{x^2+3x}\\right)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x^2+3x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(5-3x)-(5-3x)\\dfrac{d}{dx}(x^2+3x)}{(x^2+3x)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{The quotient rule}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{(x^2+3x)(-3)-(5-3x)(2x+3)}{(x^2+3x)^2}\\qquad~~~~\\gray{\\text{Differentiate }(5-3x)\\text{ \u0026 }(x^2+3x)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-3x^2-9x-(10x+15-6x^2-9x)}{(x^2+3x)^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Expand}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{-3x^2-9x-10x-15+6x^2+9x}{(x^2+3x)^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{3x^2-10x-15}{(x^2+3x)^2}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{3x^2-10x-15}{(x^2+3x)^2}$, or any other equivalent form.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $y=\\dfrac{5-3x}{x^2+3x}$.\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":"0","simplify":false,"value":"\\frac{3x^{2}-10x-15}{\\left(x^{2}+3x\\right)^{2}}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"static":false,"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
